{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:a2d70c9a2a420be5","name":"Cortosis Weave/Phrik Alloy General Template","source":{"id":"source:reference-a2d70c9a2a420be5","title":"Cortosis Weave/Phrik Alloy General Template","revision":19084,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:17:00Z","sha256":"38849ea46208da05e6d762d4fc259a4ec8a25ad560a023091821e786dc2ef0a7","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19084","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Cortosis%20Weave/Phrik%20Alloy%20General%20Template&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-a2d70c9a2a420be5","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rebellion Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rebellion_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Cost:"]}," 20% more than the base item\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Applicable To:"]}," Armor; Weapons\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["One of the hardest known substances in the galaxy, phrikite is mined at the Imperial facility on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gromas 16"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gromas_16?action=edit&redlink=1"},". When combined with tydirium it produces Phrik Alloy, which is lighter and sturdier then duralloy. Phrik also turns aside ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"},". ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapons"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Armor"}," made of Cortosis Weave or Phrik Alloy share a special property that prevents ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"}," from slicing through them with great ease.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weapons:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"}," do not ignore the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"}," of Cortosis Weave/Phrik Alloy Weapons. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Armors:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"}," do not ignore the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"}," of Cortosis Weave/Phrik Alloy Armor. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Special:"]}," During ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Old Republic Era"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Old_Republic_Era"},", almost all melee weapons are coated with a Cortosis Weave due not only to an abundance of the material, but also the presence of large numbers of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"},"-wielding combatants; as a result, they are not given the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rare"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rare"}," Availability tag during this era. During other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Eras of Play"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Eras_of_Play","referenceId":"reference:8e95f83b34b3926d"},", however, these materials are far more difficult to find, and are given the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rare"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rare"}," tag as normal.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
